WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:06.440
Did you ever wonder if certain foods
have a direct effect on your health?

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.400
Well, I’m here to
solve that mystery

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.880
since you are
the foods you eat.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.920
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.800
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.720
Today we look at the efficacy of
three widely available vaccines

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.640
and we start with a close
look at the flu vaccine,

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.640
which turns out to be
an extraordinary lifesaver.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.000
Every year,
influenza typically kills

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.520
between 4,000
and 20,000 Americans,

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.080
though the death toll
for the 2017 to 2018 season

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.080
was estimated at 80,000,

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.120
making it one of the deadliest
in the last half century.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.080
Most hospitalizations

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.620
and 90 percent
of flu-related mortality

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.560
occur in those
65 and older,

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.160
and most over the age of 75.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.160
Mortality rates for the flu
at ages 75 and older

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.240
are 50 times higher
than those below age 65.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.600
Nonetheless,
the CDC recommends

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.760
everyone over the age
of 6 months

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:07.320
get a routine annual flu shot
every year,

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.440
if for no other reason than
to help prevent transmission

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.000
to the more vulnerable.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.520
The cruel irony
is that older adults,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.520
the ones who need protection
the most,

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.960
acquire less robust protection
from flu shots

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.000
due to waning immunity with age.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.720
Depending on the season,

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.800
vaccination typically reduces
the risk of getting the flu

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.360
by about 40 to 50 percent.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.800
So, in healthy adults,

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.640
we can say
with moderate certainty

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.360
we can decrease the risk
of getting it

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.960
from like 2 percent each year
down to just under 1 percent.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.360
Among older adults,

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.680
even if you get a similar
relative risk reduction,

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.560
from 6 percent
down to 2.4 percent,

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.920
since the risk is higher
and the consequences greater,

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.200
the absolute benefits
are greater too.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.920
In the Northern Hemisphere,

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.440
the flu season can start
as early as September

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.920
and go as late as March.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.400
The problem
with getting vaccinated

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.400
too early in the season

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.960
is that immunity might wane
before the season is over,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.840
especially in older adults.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.840
So, it might be good to wait
until October,

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.720
but getting it at any time
throughout the season

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.160
is preferable to not getting
vaccinated at all.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.120
Yes, the influenza vaccine can
cause Guillain-Barré syndrome,

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.040
an autoimmune attack
on your nerves

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.840
that can leave you paralyzed
for weeks,

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.440
but so too can getting the flu.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.680
There may be
1 to 2 additional cases

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.520
of Guillain-Barré
per million vaccinations

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.000
versus about 17 extra cases
per million contacts

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.320
with the flu virus.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.120
So, you're much more likely
to be temporarily paralyzed

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.880
by the flu than the flu shot,

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:45.920
but since it takes vaccinating
about 30 older people

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.000
to prevent one case of the flu,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.920
getting vaccinated
would still, in expectation,

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.320
raise your overall
Guillain-Barré risk.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.240
But the reason flu shots
are recommended

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.920
is not to lower risk of some
obscure autoimmune syndrome

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.440
but to reduce the common,
and potentially devastating,

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:05.040
impacts of the flu
that extend well beyond

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.800
just the respiratory infection.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.920
In the week following
a confirmed flu infection,

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.360
the risk
of having a heart attack

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.760
shoots up six-fold.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.400
The inflammation of infection

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.120
can destabilize
atherosclerotic plaques,

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:19.880
constrict arteries,

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.360
and make the blood
more liable to clot.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.120
So, might flu vaccinations
save lives

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.000
in more ways than one?

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.000
That's why indirectly

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.880
the flu may kill
up to three times more.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.080
Those who get their flu shots

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.320
are indeed less likely to die
from cardiovascular disease

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.240
in a given year as well
as all causes put together.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.080
In other words, those who get
regular flu shots live,

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:44.720
on average, longer lives.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:48.120
But who disproportionally
gets flu shots?

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.880
White, married, nonsmokers
of a higher social class,

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.480
with higher education,
higher incomes,

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:55.640
and health insurance.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.640
You can't tell
if it's truly cause-and-effect

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.480
until you put it to the test.

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:04.000
There have been four
randomized controlled trials,

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.240
flu shots versus placebo shots,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:09.120
in those with
pre-existing heart disease,

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.960
and overall,
those who got the real shots

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.440
had a 56 percent lower chance
of dying

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.080
from cardiovascular disease

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:18.760
and a 47 percent lower chance
of dying

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.360
from all causes put together.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:25.680
So, flu shots really can be
an extraordinary life-saver.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.360
Whether the observational data

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.760
showing fewer deaths
across the board,

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.360
even among those without
pre-existing heart disease,

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:35.600
similarly pans out is,
as of yet, unknown,

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.480
but if you notice
for secondary prevention

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:38.880
the randomized
controlled trials

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.720
showed even more protection

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.080
than the observational studies
hinted at.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.720
Given the benefits,

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.240
overcoming vaccine hesitancy
should be as simple

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:51.600
as correcting misinformation,
but sadly,

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.840
debunking vaccine myths
may actually backfire.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.160
Busting the myth that
inactivated flu shots,

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.720
the type given to older adults,

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:00.840
can give you the flu

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:04.800
surprisingly makes people
even less likely to get it.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.880
Similarly,
correcting the falsehood

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.680
that MMR vaccines
cause autism

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.560
or that pertussis vaccination

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.560
causes as many side effects
as people think

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.200
paradoxically makes people
less inclined to vaccinate.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:21.520
The researchers conclude
"correcting vaccine myths

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:27.440
may not be an effective approach
to promoting vaccination."

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:28.600
In our next story,

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:32.520
we’ll look at how the pneumonia vaccine
significantly reduces the risk

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:37.360
of pneumococcal pneumonia
in people 65 and older.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:39.240
Vaccines are considered

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.760
one of the greatest
public health achievements

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:42.720
of the last century,

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.120
having eradicated smallpox,

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.880
a scourge that killed
hundreds of millions of people,

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.080
and greatly reducing
other major diseases,

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.120
such as measles and polio.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.320
To this day,
vaccines are estimated

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:58.680
to save millions of lives
a year.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.200
More than 90 percent
of U.S. children

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.200
get common
childhood vaccinations,

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:06.640
such as polio or their measles,
mumps, and rubella shot,

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.920
but most adults fail
to get their full complement

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:11.480
of recommended
adult vaccinations.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:14.520
Assuming you got
all your childhood vaccinations,

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:16.680
and aside from
any emergent pandemic needs,

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.800
the CDC recommends
all healthy adults

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:20.760
get annual flu shots,

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.720
tetanus boosters
every ten years,

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:24.160
though the World Health
Organization

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.120
doesn't think
this is necessary,

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:29.160
shingles vaccination
at age 50,

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.960
and pneumonia vaccine
at age 65.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:34.320
Certain groups need others,

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.160
such as a hepatitis B series
for healthcare workers

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.280
or men who have sex with men.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:43.480
Ask your medical professional
for a personalized schedule.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:46.360
How safe are vaccines?

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.560
In a systematic review
and meta-analysis,

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:52.720
the RAND Corporation screened
more than 50,000 citations

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.560
and concluded
that routine vaccinations

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:56.840
can be considered safe,

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:59.640
with only rare
serious adverse effects,

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.360
such as severe
allergic reactions,

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.200
in 1 to 10 in a million,

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:06.040
and transient autoimmune
syndromes Guillain-BarrĂ©

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.440
and immune
thrombocytopenic purpura

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:09.840
in 1 to 3 in a million,

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.160
and 10 to 30 in a million

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:16.040
for flu shots and MMR vaccines,
respectively.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:18.880
Of course, any adverse effects
should be weighed against

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:22.295
any protective effects
that vaccines may provide.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:25.120
What about pneumonia vaccines?

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:28.240
"Pneumonia may well be called
the friend of the aged,"

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.040
wrote the "Father
of Modern Medicine,"

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:31.520
Sir William Osler,

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:34.720
over a hundred years ago
in 1898.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.000
"Taken off by it
in an acute, short,

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.440
not often painful illness,

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:42.080
the old man escapes those
'cold gradations of decay'

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:45.480
so distressing to himself
and to his friends."

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.600
The thought
was that pneumonia

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:50.040
mercifully killed those
who would soon die anyway

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:53.160
from potentially a more
protracted, painful illness.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.080
But, these days,

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.360
healthy older adults
hospitalized for pneumonia

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:58.720
are not significantly
more likely to die

00:07:58.720 --> 00:07:59.960
in the subsequent two years

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:03.160
than younger adults
in the same situation.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:06.160
Because of comorbidities
at older ages, though,

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:09.240
pneumonia is the fourth leading
cause of death in the world

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:12.920
and the ninth leading cause
in the United States.

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:16.400
The most common cause of
community-acquired pneumonia,

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.360
as opposed to hospital-acquired,

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.880
is a bacteria
known as pneumococcus,

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:23.320
or Streptococcus pneumoniae.

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:24.640
In addition to pneumonia,

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:27.560
pneumococcus can cause
inner ear infections,

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:28.880
sinusitis, or pinkeye.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:33.160
It gets serious when it starts
to invade the bloodstream,

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:36.280
which can result in meningitis,
infection of the brain;

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:38.640
endocarditis,
infection of the heart valves;

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:41.760
or sepsis, a life-threatening
organ dysfunction

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:43.720
caused by blood poisoning.

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:47.640
Thankfully, we have vaccines
against pneumococcus.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:50.080
The first was developed
over a century ago,

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:53.000
but they fell out of favor
after penicillin was discovered,

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:56.120
thinking antibiotics
would eliminate the threat.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:58.800
Unfortunately,
these days up to 40 percent

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.800
of these kind
of streptococcal infections

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:04.000
are resistant
to at least one antibiotic,

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.680
and despite our miracle drugs,

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:07.760
mortality rates
of invasive pneumococcus

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:12.120
in the elderly remain
around 15 to 30 percent.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:14.040
However,
randomized controlled trials

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:16.280
have found
that pneumococcus vaccines

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:18.400
reduce the risk
of those 65 and older

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:21.320
getting pneumococcal pneumonia
by 64 percent,

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:22.680
and, even more importantly,

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.920
your risk of invasive
pneumococcal disease

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:26.720
by 73 percent.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.280
Like the flu vaccine,

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:30.720
population studies have found
that pneumonia vaccines

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:33.120
can reduce the risk
of both heart attacks

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:36.560
and the overall risk of dying,
but unlike flu vaccines,

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.560
there aren't randomized
controlled trials

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:42.040
to confirm
these bonus benefits.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:42.800
Finally today,

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:45.120
we’ll discover how
the new shingles vaccine

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.960
compares with
the previous one.

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:49.720
Adult vaccination
can be thought of

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:52.400
as a cornerstone
of successful aging,

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:53.480
but a major issue

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:56.400
hampering the uptake
of shingles vaccination

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:59.080
is the lack of awareness
of the disease.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:01.520
Shingles is caused
by a reactivation

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:04.160
of the chicken pox virus
later in life.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.320
After your body
beats back chicken pox,

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:09.240
the virus hides in waiting
in your spinal cord,

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:12.240
waiting for an opportunity
to strike back.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:14.640
When it does,
the virus can surge forth,

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:16.920
traveling along the path
of a nerve

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.040
branching off the spinal cord,

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:20.800
wrapping around one side
of the body to the front,

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.520
producing skin blisters
along the way

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:24.840
in a characteristic
belt-like pattern

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:27.840
that does not cross
the midline in front.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:30.840
Both shingles and the name
of the virus, zoster,

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:33.720
are from the Latin and Greek,
respectively, for "belt".

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:36.580
The blistering rash
can be intensely painful

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:38.760
and leave scarring
or discoloration behind,

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:42.040
but usually disappears
in a few weeks on its own.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.280
However, approximately 30
to 50 percent of people suffer

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:46.960
"postherpetic neuralgia,"

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:50.520
persistent pain that can last
for a year or more,

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:53.360
that sometimes
can be debilitating.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:56.000
Usually, it affects nerves
around your trunk,

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.840
but in 10 to 25 percent
of cases,

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:00.680
it can erupt across your face,

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:03.360
which can lead to permanent
facial muscle weakness,

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:06.600
hearing loss,
or blindness.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.160
As if that's all
not bad enough,

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:11.280
having shingles as much
as quintuples your odds

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:14.360
of having a stroke
over the subsequent few weeks,

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:15.960
a risk that gradually declines

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:19.040
over the following
six to twelve months.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:21.640
It's surprising more people
don't know about it,

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:24.880
since the lifetime risk
of shingles is 30 percent.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:26.880
Meaning nearly one in three
will get it

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.720
sometime in their lives.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.520
Young adults only have
about a 1 in 1,000 chance

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:32.720
of getting it every year,

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:34.080
whereas in older adults

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:37.640
that climbs to closer
to 1 in 100 each year.

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:40.160
That comes out
to a million cases of shingles

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:42.960
every year
in the United States.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:46.120
Thankfully,
there is a shingles vaccine.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:48.000
The first became available
in 2006,

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.840
using a live weakened strain
of the virus.

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:53.720
The efficacy
was only about 50 percent

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:56.880
and couldn't be used in
immunocompromised individuals,

00:11:56.880 --> 00:12:00.280
such as those with HIV
or on immunosuppressive drugs,

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.240
such as many on chemotherapy.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:03.920
Thankfully, in 2017,

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:06.040
a recombinant
shingles vaccine was approved

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:10.720
with a 90 to 97 percent efficacy
for preventing an outbreak.

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:12.520
It requires
two separate injections

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:13.920
2 to 6 months apart,

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.200
and is expensive,
like 280 bucks,

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.440
but covered by Medicare

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:20.160
and most private
insurance plans.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:22.640
It also can cause
transient systemic symptoms,

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:24.720
such as muscle aches,
fatigue, headaches,

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:26.960
or fever and chills
serious enough to interfere

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:30.320
with everyday activities
about 10 percent of the time,

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:32.000
but the new vaccine
is considered

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.680
so much more effective
that it's recommended

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:36.560
for everyone
starting at age 50,

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:40.120
even if you were previously
immunized with the old one.

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:43.800
Given that the new vaccine
is only about five years old,

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:46.640
longer-term safety
and efficacy data

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.960
is still coming in,
but, so far so good.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:54.400
As soon as I turned 50,
I lined up for mine.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:56.560
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:12:56.560 --> 00:13:00.040
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.720
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:06.880
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:10.840
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:14.360
please go to the Nutrition Facts
Podcast landing page.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:16.740
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:20.720
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite for each of these topics.

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:23.280
My latest book, “How Not to Age”
is out now,

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:27.000
which premiered at #2 on the
New York Times Best Sellers list.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.320
Check it out at your
local public library.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:31.640
Of course, all the proceeds
I receive of the sales

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:35.400
of all my books goes
directly to charity.

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:40.080
NutritionFacts.org is itself a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:41.880
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:45.920
on the latest in nutrition research
via bite-sized videos and articles.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:48.240
Everything on the
website is free.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:49.240
There’s no ads,

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:50.920
no corporate sponsorships,
no kickbacks.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:54.160
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:57.240
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:59.640
as a tribute to
my grandmother,

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:04.833
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

